  "implementation": [
    "Managed installation ID and existing owner credential persist across keyed/interactive enrollment and disconnect. Tailnet changes do not rotate this local ownership credential.",
    "Pending managed sign-in requires the existing owner; token-free legacy pending first use remains unchanged.",
    "Lost provision/disconnect replies are recoverable using the already-held owner token, including after reload. Rejected auth-key joins return to local-only control.",
    "Managed signout atomically saves local-only configuration before retiring the owned PD session/arm gate and waiting for logout. Failed persistence preserves the session and owner.",
    "Managed rejoin retires the owned PD session even when its local token is unchanged. No automatic DSP restart, calibration rearm or RF.",
    "Login generation fencing discards pre-disconnect URLs while keeping the valid local owner credential.",
    "Status managed_owner_version1 advertises the new contract. The desktop refuses enrollment for older/unknown managed contracts and malformed installation IDs, with an available-reason hint.",
    "Opening Remote Access can enroll a supported managed local installation only after loading its owner token, on the LAN, once per window/Refresh. Pending sign-in is read, not replaced.",
    "Legacy Reset/Update actions refuse managed installations; unavailable owner recovery is stated instead of proposing the legacy waveform reinstall."
  ],
